            <ArticleTitle>[Two pulmonary lesions on an X-ray of the chest].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>D1815</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present an X-ray of a 89-year-old man, showing two solitary pulmonary lesions. Although malignancy was suspected, these lesions appeared to be intrafissural pleural effusions, caused by congestive heart failure. One week after treatment with furosemide, the pulmonary lesions had disappeared completely.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
